  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2e811ff2e3d71e44497d87cf957c8c63, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsConfig
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Holobiont.InstructionsConfig
  controlsText: "<b>W / S</b> \u2014 Faster / slower breathing rhythm.\n<b>D / A</b>
    \u2014 Deeper / shallower breath (grows or shrinks the field).\n<b>Space (hold)</b>
    \u2014 Hold the breath at the current point in the cycle.\n  \u2022 hold mid-exhale
    \u2192 bonds any unbound creatures inside the field\n  \u2022 hold mid-inhale
    \u2192 releases your most-stressed bonded creature\n  \u2022 release into the
    opposite phase to boost the next breath\n<b>Esc</b> \u2014 Pause menu.\n\nPushing
    parameters off baseline or holding too long drains stamina \u2014 bottom out
    and you're locked into a forced recovery with no input."
  howToPlayText: "You are a holobiont \u2014 a colony bound by breath. Survive as
    long as you can.\n\nYour field breathes on its own. On every exhale it pulls
    free creatures toward you; on every inhale it pushes them away. Shape the rhythm
    with WASD \u2014 deeper breaths reach further, faster ones cycle quicker \u2014
    and hold Space at the right moment to bond a creature (mid-exhale) or release
    one (mid-inhale). Three types matter:\n\n  \u2022 <b>Nutrici</b> \u2014 convert
    your breath into energy.\n  \u2022 <b>Scudo</b> \u2014 shield you from environmental
    stress (temperature, light, humidity, toxicity).\n  \u2022 <b>Hub</b> \u2014
    raise your energy capacity and creature slots.\n\nEnergy drains every second
    from upkeep, creature stress, and mismatch between your resistances and the drifting
    environment. Bond Nutrici to stay in the black, Scudo to survive shifts, and
    shed stressed creatures before they die. If energy hits zero, the colony cascades
    and dies."
